@*
    The atmosphere behind a hero.

    One component, used by every page that needs one, because the three that came before it each
    drew their own floor: a 72px graticule here, an 18px rack rhythm there, a wireframe elevation
    over the top, each masked differently. Individually each was defensible. Together they made
    the site look like three products, and every one of them put hard geometry behind type.

    What is left is light. Two soft pools placed off-centre so the composition has a direction,
    and nothing with an edge. Depth comes from the gradient falling off, not from a shape drawn
    on top of the page.

    Decorative and nothing else, so it is hidden from assistive technology and cannot be hit by
    a pointer.
*@

<div class="ambient @Variant" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="pool pool--brand"></span>
    <span class="pool pool--tech"></span>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Where the light sits, so two pages in a row do not open identically.</summary>
    public enum FieldVariant
    {
        /// <summary>Light gathered to the right, under a product visual.</summary>
        Right,

        /// <summary>Light gathered to the left.</summary>
        Left,

        /// <summary>Light gathered behind the middle, for a centred composition.</summary>
        Centre,
    }

    /// <summary>Which arrangement to draw.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public FieldVariant Placement { get; set; } = FieldVariant.Right;

    private string Variant => Placement switch
    {
        FieldVariant.Left => "is-left",
        FieldVariant.Centre => "is-centre",
        _ => "is-right",
    };
}

